      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subtle, sudden instability in high racks, even when the load seems secure, often points toward external disturbances. Vibrations are a prime suspect, especially if you have heavy forklifts or other machinery moving through those aisles. Even a slight, rhythmic vibration—like a poorly maintained conveyor or a nearby heavy vehicle—can cause the entire stack to \"walk\" or settle unevenly. It's a delicate balance, and these subtle movements can be enough to overcome the static friction holding a top-tier load in place. You might need to check the floor mounting of your racking to see if it's absorbing vibrations effectively.",
